963]]}, {"t": "DC", "lp": -9.811405470827594e-05, "top": [["DC", -9.811405470827594e-05], [" DC", -10.523123741149902]]}, {"t": "MAKE", "lp": -6.616334576392546e-05, "top": [["MAKE", -6.616334576392546e-05], ["Make", -10.453043937683105]]}, {"t": "_C", "lp": -0.002439133357256651, "top": [["_C", -0.002439133357256651], ["_X", -6.976150989532471]]}, {"t": "XX", "lp": -0.00011552047362783924, "top": [["XX", -0.00011552047362783924], ["_COMPILER", -10.168787956237793]]}, {"t": "_COMPILER", "lp": -0.0003421891888137907, "top": [["_COMPILER", -0.0003421891888137907], [" Compiler", -9.970995903015137]]}, {"t": "=", "lp": -0.00032895253389142454, "top": [["=", -0.00032895253389142454], [" ic", -11.284890174865723]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -1.8239186829305254e-05, "top": [["ic", -1.8239186829305254e-05], [" ic", -11.387541770935059]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're using Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, which aren't on the default PATH.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero (error) status. A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into broken output.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S` \u2014 **S**ource directory (the cloned llama.cpp repo)\n- `-B` \u2014 **B**uild directory (where build artifacts go)\n- `-G Ninja` \u2014 Use the **Ninja** build system (fast, minimal output) instead of the default Makefiles\n\n## Build Type & Installation\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimize for performance (enables `-O3`-level optimizations). Not `Debug` (which would add symbols and slow the binary).\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install prefix: `/usr` (standard system location)\n- Library directory: `lib` (not `lib64`, which some distros use)\n\n## The Compilers\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=ic"}